commit bdc6e37300a487dead4c95740204164a82278acb
Author: cracki <cracki@gmail.com>
Date:   Wed Oct 7 15:53:36 2026 +0330

    fix(qa4-MOM): copy-on-write brand data, payload scrubbing, upload + domain validation
    
    MOM half-done/not-done items closed (implementation verified by two
    independent agents):
    - Scraped site data no longer shared between users: BrandWebsiteData and
      BrandCoreAnalysis gain a nullable brand FK (migration 0016); analysis
      lookups scope to the asking brand first, fall back to the shared
      identity row read-only; force_refresh writes a brand-owned row and
      never mutates a row owned by another brand (full_analysis.py copy-
      on-write; tests prove user A's refresh leaves user B's data intact).
    - Raw payloads scrubbed: ad_library AdLibraryRunSerializer and market
      run serializers strip internal keys (prompt/system_prompt/raw/debug/
      error internals) at any depth via to_representation; FE-consumed
      business keys and input_snapshot/request_payload verified against the
      frontend and kept. market failing runs persist a generic error
      message + logger.exception instead of str(exc) leaks.
    - Upload validation: BrandAssetUploadSerializer enforces
      png/jpeg/webp/svg/pdf + 5MB cap.
    - Domain hardening: localhost/127.0.0.1/private IPs/.local/.internal
      rejected as brand website_url (serializer field error).
    - brand/tests.py: one assertion updated for the scrubbed payload.
    - Tests: brand 9 + ad_library 3 + market 3 new, all green.

